From 3b2fc784fb916a967ffbb1c222eedf1955ebd8ed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FiyeroT <me@fiyero.xyz>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 21:07:03 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 33/88] urltest: test a member out of turn when a connection
 gets no answer

A Hysteria2 or TUIC server that went silent still opens streams, and a VLESS or
Trojan server whose own outbound is dead still accepts and handshakes: the dial
and the first write succeed and the answer never comes, so the group saw nothing
until its periodic test. The group now watches the first answer of every TCP
connection through a member. A connection is overdue when no byte has come one
retransmission timeout after the client's last write, the timeout computed as
RFC 6298 does from the member's own first-byte latencies (seeded with its URL
test delay) plus one retransmitted SYN on the server's side, at most the TCP
timeout of sing-box; a late answer gives no sample and doubles the timeout
(Karn). A connection that fails on the way before the first byte (reset, abort,
a timeout no deadline of the caller set) counts at once; an EOF or an error the
server sent back does not. An overdue connection is refuted by an answer to a
later connection or by a test of the member that began later; otherwise the
confirmation test decides, with pauses kept apart from those of failed dials,
and a destination that stayed silent while the member passed counts no more for
an interval. Once the group has switched away from a member that lost its test
result, the member's connections that never got an answer are closed. The
watching connection passes the read waiter of the connection below through, so
a connection waiting for its first byte holds no buffer either; times are
monotonic offsets from the epoch of the group.

Lab, member silent from t=15 s: Hysteria2 connections failed until 27 s (41 s
before on 1.14, the group never left the member within 60 s on 1.13 before S1
counted QUIC timeouts); VLESS with a dead exit until 26-28 s (the periodic test,
up to 3 min, before). A quiet router whose only traffic went to one dead site
made one test in 60 s and no switch; 5% loss and tls_fragment made none.
